      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Relying on self-monitoring for blood clotting risks is unsafe because your INR (blood-thinning level) can fluctuate unpredictably even with tiny amounts of Vitamin K, and a weakened clotting balance may cause a significant bleed or fatal stroke. While vitamins are natural, they still interact pharmacologically with medications, and your doctor prescribed the lower Vitamin K requirement intentionally for this exact reason. Please contact your clinic today to get a clear dose limit or alternative plan before your next check-up.",
      "source": "target",
